fier":"D","content":"1"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"The energy of an electron in an excited state of hydrogen is given by the equation:\n<br><br>\nCode snippet<br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.871ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"17.241ex\" height=\"2.828ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 7620.5 1250.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1041.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2097.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2875.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(4653.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(409.7,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(220,-377.4) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(633,289) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"933\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5826.5,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"65\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-65\"></use><use data-c=\"56\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-56\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br><br>\nwhere n is the principal quantum number of the state.\n<br><br>\nThe energy of the electron beam is 12.5 eV, which is enough to excite the electron to the n = 3 state.<br><br> The possible transitions from n = 3 to lower energy states are:\n<br><br>\nn = 3 to n = 2, with a wavelength of 656.33 nm (H-alpha)<br><br>\nn = 3 to n = 1, with a wavelength of 102.57 nm (Lyman-alpha)<br><br>\nn = 2 to n = 1, with a wavelength of 121.57 nm (Lyman-beta)<br><br>\nTherefore, there are 3 possible spectral lines that can be emitted.","exam":"jee-main","questions":[{"question_id":"pa-125-mathrmev-electron-beam-is-used-to-bombard-jee-main-physics-motion-gco9fw7gij704qhw","qKey":"pa-125-mathrmev-electron-beam-is-used-to-bombard-jee-main-physics-motion-gco9fw7gij704qhw","permalink":"pa-125-mathrmev-electron-beam-is-used-to-bombard-jee-main-physics-motion-gco9fw7gij704qhw","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 12th April Morning Shift","year":2023,"subject":"physics","chapter":"atoms-and-nuclei","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>A <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.081ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 3572 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><us